Alireza, thanks for your email.  The problem is that the declarations made inside the nimbleCode function (the nimble model declaration) specifically these:

+   I.rhoW <- diag(N)- (rho*distMat)

+   inv <- inverse(I.rhoW)

+   inv.X <- inv %*% X.mat

do not create these objects in the R workspace.  In order to be able to use "inv.X" in the data list (for the "data" argument to nimbleModel function, I presume), you would need to include these lines of R code *outside* of the nimbleCode function, as regular R code, something akin to:

rho <- [some value]
### you already declared N and distMat, so that's fine

I.rhoW <- diag(N)- (rho*distMat)
inv <- inverse(I.rhoW)

## you already declared X.mat, so that's fine

inv.X <- inv %*% X.mat

> SLMMdata <- list(y = baltimore$PRICE, T1 = inv.X[,1],
+                  T2 = inv.X[,2], T3 = inv.X[,3],
+                  T4 = inv.X[,4], T5 = inv.X[,5],
+                  T6 = inv.X[,6], T7 = inv.X[,7],
+                  T8 = inv.X[,8], T9 = inv.X[,9],
+                  Dist = distMat)

I hope this helps.  Keep in touch.  You might consider looking at the Nimble User Manual, which is available online.

Daniel

